1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Threatened by a ruthless demon, humanity was on the brink of destruction.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,000
All seemed lost until a lone mage stepped forward and took up the fight.

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:28,000
After his triumph, he was hailed as the Wizard King, and his story became legend.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Round one, match six of the Royal Knight Selection Exam.

5
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Steel creation magic, full metal fortress!

6
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:41,000
Lightning magic, thunderbolt destruction!

7
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Gotcha!

8
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Weight magic!

9
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Angel flapping ought to do the trick!

10
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:49,000
Go for it!

11
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Oh boy, this is a lot of fun!

12
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:54,000
More!

13
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Let's fight some more!

14
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:01,000
Thanks to their fine teamwork and Luck's unexpected increase in strength, Team K won their match.

15
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Then, in the eighth and final match of round one...

16
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:07,000
It's gonna be Yuno and Noelle on a team together!

17
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:09,000
Can we please not do this?

18
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:12,000
The Silver House is divided. Noelle versus Solid.

19
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:22,000
Meanwhile, the bad blood between Alecdora and Yuno, born of a festering jealousy over Vongence's respect for the commoner, erupts into a full-blown grudge match between the two.

20
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:26,000
I will be the one to bring Sir Vongence's dream into reality!

21
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:28,000
Wind magic!

22
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Towering tornado!

23
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:34,000
Why would I care about someone else's dream?

24
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:36,000
I only fight...

25
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:38,000
For my own dream.

26
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Sea Dragon's Roar!

27
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:46,000
Crystal destroyed! Team P wins!

28
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:48,000
I'm not weak!

29
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:49,000
Not anymore!

30
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:01,000
Not any sign in.

31
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:02,000
ibly

32
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:03,000
Not idea in the world.

33
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:05,000
He's when he wants me.

34
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:12,000
Remember,

35
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:17,000
With his hands,

36
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:18,920
Too ниbe

37
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:23,000
Trouble…

38
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:52,980
We'll be right back.

39
00:02:53,000 --> 00:03:22,980
We'll be right back.

40
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:25,000
We'll be right back.

41
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:26,040
This can't be.

42
00:03:26,720 --> 00:03:28,020
There's no way.

43
00:03:30,880 --> 00:03:32,980
Yuno managed to defeat my best spell.

44
00:03:33,260 --> 00:03:34,440
He made it look like nothing.

45
00:03:34,860 --> 00:03:36,620
He didn't even use his spirit magic.

46
00:03:37,500 --> 00:03:39,080
All that power and he was still

47
00:03:39,080 --> 00:03:39,820
halting back.

48
00:03:40,540 --> 00:03:42,960
I will make Sir Vangeance's dream come true.

49
00:03:45,640 --> 00:03:47,420
Here's the thing about you nobles.

50
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:49,660
When you stumble, you break.

51
00:03:50,820 --> 00:03:51,340
Yeah!

52
00:03:51,540 --> 00:03:52,960
That was an awesome fight, Yuno!

53
00:03:53,660 --> 00:03:55,240
Same to you, Shortstack.

54
00:03:55,340 --> 00:03:56,760
Now you're calling me that!

55
00:03:57,040 --> 00:03:58,860
That was super cool, Yuno!

56
00:03:58,860 --> 00:04:01,940
I could watch you fight like that all day long!

57
00:04:02,180 --> 00:04:04,740
Here, I brought your usual post-battle dessert!

58
00:04:05,460 --> 00:04:07,100
It would help me keep up my stamina.

59
00:04:09,680 --> 00:04:10,780
Thank you for this.

60
00:04:11,040 --> 00:04:12,100
It's just what I needed.

61
00:04:12,600 --> 00:04:13,740
Thank you for this.

62
00:04:14,020 --> 00:04:15,300
It's just what I needed.

63
00:04:15,300 --> 00:04:20,720
It's delicious.

64
00:04:25,800 --> 00:04:26,740
Hey, Charmy!

65
00:04:26,900 --> 00:04:27,640
You feeling okay?

66
00:04:30,160 --> 00:04:31,440
Oh, come on, Spinehead!

67
00:04:31,520 --> 00:04:32,300
Get over yourself!

68
00:04:32,400 --> 00:04:33,200
That meant nothing!

69
00:04:33,640 --> 00:04:35,080
Shut up, or I will step your nose

70
00:04:35,080 --> 00:04:36,440
and struggle so you suffocate!

71
00:04:36,580 --> 00:04:37,160
You hear me?

72
00:04:37,400 --> 00:04:38,200
Take that!

73
00:04:38,880 --> 00:04:40,080
I guess you're good.

74
00:04:40,080 --> 00:04:42,660
Hey there.

75
00:04:42,880 --> 00:04:45,160
So listen, just wanted to say you were great.

76
00:04:45,560 --> 00:04:48,000
Honestly, I had no idea you were that powerful.

77
00:04:48,340 --> 00:04:50,760
I feel like your personality changes quite a bit

78
00:04:50,760 --> 00:04:52,360
when you're not doing the mushroom thing.

79
00:04:53,100 --> 00:04:53,820
But still.

80
00:04:54,680 --> 00:04:58,060
I've been listening to Solid since before the battle began.

81
00:04:58,400 --> 00:05:01,620
The way that monster treats his baby sister is unacceptable.

82
00:05:03,340 --> 00:05:06,220
Noel, an older brother's most important job

83
00:05:06,220 --> 00:05:08,760
is to look after his siblings who are younger and weaker.

84
00:05:08,760 --> 00:05:12,180
But judging by the many hurtful things I've heard him say,

85
00:05:12,300 --> 00:05:14,880
it doesn't sound like he's even trying to uphold that responsibility.

86
00:05:15,120 --> 00:05:16,720
So thrash him once and for all!

87
00:05:17,600 --> 00:05:19,580
Um, thank you...

88
00:05:19,580 --> 00:05:20,900
for what you said back there.

89
00:05:23,840 --> 00:05:25,680
You did great work.

90
00:05:27,100 --> 00:05:29,040
You know, that's a bit patronizing.

91
00:05:29,440 --> 00:05:30,820
I am still royalty.

92
00:05:33,280 --> 00:05:35,240
Let's do our best next time, too.

93
00:05:35,240 --> 00:05:38,980
That monoskin training I did really helped me to regulate my magic.

94
00:05:40,100 --> 00:05:41,820
I just have to keep this up,

95
00:05:42,040 --> 00:05:43,900
and I'll be chosen as a royal knight!

96
00:05:44,980 --> 00:05:45,320
Whew!

97
00:05:45,580 --> 00:05:47,680
Those matches were really something else.

98
00:05:48,240 --> 00:05:49,820
I can't wait for the next ones.

99
00:05:50,360 --> 00:05:52,200
Yes, I require more amusement.

100
00:05:53,900 --> 00:05:56,520
It's a shame that the two commoders who embarrass me

101
00:05:56,520 --> 00:05:57,600
are still in the running.

102
00:05:58,260 --> 00:06:00,020
Why won't they just lose?

103
00:06:00,020 --> 00:06:01,460
All right, then.

104
00:06:01,620 --> 00:06:03,260
Let's move on to the second round.

105
00:06:03,740 --> 00:06:06,020
Oh, but before we start...

106
00:06:06,020 --> 00:06:07,060
Go ahead.

107
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:08,260
You know what to do.

108
00:06:08,360 --> 00:06:08,680
Sir!

109
00:06:20,560 --> 00:06:21,000
Whoa!

110
00:06:21,380 --> 00:06:22,160
The field!

111
00:06:22,420 --> 00:06:24,240
It's shifting right in front of us!

112
00:06:24,720 --> 00:06:25,880
So cool!

113
00:06:25,880 --> 00:06:30,300
For us to get a good sense of your abilities,

114
00:06:30,460 --> 00:06:32,840
we need to see you fight in various circumstances.

115
00:06:36,260 --> 00:06:37,260
Hey, I'm back!

116
00:06:37,440 --> 00:06:38,060
Hello there.

117
00:06:39,300 --> 00:06:40,420
Take a good look.

118
00:06:40,860 --> 00:06:43,660
This is the stage on which round two will be fought.

119
00:06:47,100 --> 00:06:49,260
They can change the stage all they like,

120
00:06:49,340 --> 00:06:51,140
but my beauty shall remain constant.

121
00:06:51,460 --> 00:06:52,260
Yeah, yeah.

122
00:06:52,260 --> 00:06:55,200
Oh, as for this bit of human waste,

123
00:06:55,900 --> 00:06:58,740
I'll wipe you away like the unsightly stain you are.

124
00:06:58,800 --> 00:07:00,740
You'll find out I'm stickier than you think!

125
00:07:00,900 --> 00:07:01,960
Talk trash all you want,

126
00:07:02,020 --> 00:07:03,960
but Asta's strong and he has me with him.

127
00:07:04,180 --> 00:07:06,660
So you're the one who's about to get wiped away, brother.

128
00:07:06,960 --> 00:07:07,660
Hey, Asta!

129
00:07:08,140 --> 00:07:09,940
You better not pull any punches with me.

130
00:07:10,380 --> 00:07:11,540
Not a chance, Magna!

131
00:07:11,580 --> 00:07:12,580
I'm kicking your butt!

132
00:07:12,900 --> 00:07:15,180
I hope he doesn't break your ugly purple glasses.

133
00:07:15,500 --> 00:07:17,280
Shut your freakishly big face, lady.

134
00:07:18,360 --> 00:07:19,100
Oh my.

135
00:07:19,100 --> 00:07:20,900
It looks like we're up against royalty.

136
00:07:20,900 --> 00:07:24,820
I guess we'll just have to keep relying on that teamwork, huh?

137
00:07:26,580 --> 00:07:27,740
You're laughing now,

138
00:07:27,840 --> 00:07:29,680
but you looked worried when the field shifted.

139
00:07:30,020 --> 00:07:30,840
So be honest.

140
00:07:31,220 --> 00:07:33,860
You rigged the field with traps again this round, didn't you?

141
00:07:34,960 --> 00:07:35,760
That's weird.

142
00:07:36,120 --> 00:07:36,760
How'd he know?

143
00:07:37,400 --> 00:07:39,840
I guess he must have picked up on some key or something.

144
00:07:42,320 --> 00:07:44,020
All right, yeah, I did.

145
00:07:44,740 --> 00:07:46,280
I came out here yesterday

146
00:07:46,280 --> 00:07:48,800
and scattered a bunch of traps around the stage.

147
00:07:48,800 --> 00:07:51,500
My intel told me this was where the test would be,

148
00:07:51,660 --> 00:07:53,480
so I took advantage of that knowledge.

149
00:07:54,480 --> 00:07:55,580
His intel?

150
00:07:55,860 --> 00:07:57,860
But the location of the Royal Knight's exam

151
00:07:57,860 --> 00:08:00,080
should be highly classified information.

152
00:08:01,140 --> 00:08:02,500
What could his source be?

153
00:08:02,660 --> 00:08:04,340
You placed the traps yesterday?

154
00:08:04,680 --> 00:08:06,660
That's playing dirty, you stupid jerk!

155
00:08:06,660 --> 00:08:09,160
It's part of the game, you idiot.

156
00:08:09,380 --> 00:08:09,620
What?

157
00:08:09,780 --> 00:08:11,620
Haven't you heard of information warfare?

158
00:08:12,340 --> 00:08:13,840
Did you see something in the rules

159
00:08:13,840 --> 00:08:15,780
saying not to set traps the day before?

160
00:08:16,200 --> 00:08:16,560
Huh?

161
00:08:17,100 --> 00:08:19,280
No one's yelled at me about it except you.

162
00:08:19,540 --> 00:08:21,020
Hey, dude, stop!

163
00:08:21,280 --> 00:08:21,680
Stop!

164
00:08:21,800 --> 00:08:23,160
He won that argument fast!

165
00:08:23,160 --> 00:08:24,160
Come on, let go!

166
00:08:24,400 --> 00:08:26,380
Lost is so cute when he's mad!

167
00:08:26,380 --> 00:08:28,840
Okay, then at least let us know where the traps are

168
00:08:28,840 --> 00:08:30,260
so we can coordinate with you!

169
00:08:30,420 --> 00:08:31,320
We'll work together!

170
00:08:32,460 --> 00:08:33,360
Not happening.

171
00:08:33,840 --> 00:08:36,420
You'd probably give it away to the enemy by accident.

172
00:08:37,180 --> 00:08:39,080
I mean, he's not wrong.

173
00:08:39,600 --> 00:08:41,360
Look, I've got my way of fighting

174
00:08:41,360 --> 00:08:42,480
and I'm sticking to it.

175
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:42,780
Man!

176
00:08:44,060 --> 00:08:44,500
Fine!

177
00:08:44,720 --> 00:08:46,000
But if you're doing this your way,

178
00:08:46,040 --> 00:08:48,100
then you'd better believe that I'm gonna do the same!

179
00:08:48,680 --> 00:08:50,720
It looks like they're having a bit of an argument.

180
00:08:51,100 --> 00:08:52,660
I hope it isn't anything serious.

181
00:08:52,660 --> 00:08:55,800
They say that constant pickering is the truest sign of friendship.

182
00:08:56,040 --> 00:08:57,980
I hope we'll have an argument ourselves someday.

183
00:08:58,340 --> 00:09:00,940
Do you expect me to believe you'll come up with your own plan

184
00:09:00,940 --> 00:09:02,620
with that puny little brain of yours?

185
00:09:02,720 --> 00:09:03,220
No way.

186
00:09:04,600 --> 00:09:07,060
Hey, I've got more brains than I know what to do with!

187
00:09:07,080 --> 00:09:07,520
That's right!

188
00:09:07,600 --> 00:09:08,460
You tell him, Asta!

189
00:09:08,520 --> 00:09:10,440
The only small thing about you is your stature!

190
00:09:10,580 --> 00:09:11,580
Yeah, so...

191
00:09:11,580 --> 00:09:12,440
Hold on, what?

192
00:09:14,540 --> 00:09:15,360
Your attention!

193
00:09:15,880 --> 00:09:16,520
Team B!

194
00:09:16,780 --> 00:09:18,480
Xerx, Mimosa, and Asta!

195
00:09:19,180 --> 00:09:20,280
Versus Team C!

196
00:09:20,540 --> 00:09:22,160
Kirsch, Sol, and Magna!

197
00:09:22,160 --> 00:09:24,660
Round two, match one, begin!

198
00:09:34,880 --> 00:09:38,060
Mimosa, you've stood by these peasants for too long,

199
00:09:38,180 --> 00:09:40,260
allowing their crude mana to taint your own.

200
00:09:40,540 --> 00:09:41,740
What a sad sight.

201
00:09:42,140 --> 00:09:43,400
But fear not, sweet sister,

202
00:09:43,500 --> 00:09:45,840
I'll release you from the grasp of these filthy beasts

203
00:09:45,840 --> 00:09:47,320
before any of you can fight.

204
00:09:47,320 --> 00:09:56,120
Cherry Blossom Magic!

205
00:09:56,540 --> 00:09:58,980
Raging Magic Cherry Blossom Storm of Petals!

206
00:09:59,340 --> 00:10:01,020
Plus my beautiful illusion!

207
00:10:01,020 --> 00:10:06,320
Well now, that's quite a view.

208
00:10:06,640 --> 00:10:07,320
So pretty!

209
00:10:07,720 --> 00:10:09,560
This goes for a celebratory snack!

210
00:10:10,240 --> 00:10:11,600
And for you!

211
00:10:11,600 --> 00:10:16,360
Now, in the embrace of my most beautiful spell,

212
00:10:16,720 --> 00:10:19,520
you're free to relinquish your soiled past self!

213
00:10:19,520 --> 00:10:24,580
I know I topped big a minute ago,

214
00:10:24,700 --> 00:10:26,180
but as hard as I've been training

215
00:10:26,180 --> 00:10:27,620
and as much as I've improved,

216
00:10:27,780 --> 00:10:30,440
I don't think I have a single spell that can counter this.

217
00:10:30,980 --> 00:10:32,760
We shouldn't be hasty to act.

218
00:10:33,200 --> 00:10:36,340
Our best bet is to sit tight and wait for them to set off a trap.

219
00:10:36,700 --> 00:10:38,060
What an amazing spell!

220
00:10:38,640 --> 00:10:40,280
I can't see a thing right now.

221
00:10:41,560 --> 00:10:43,380
This might be our only way out.

222
00:10:43,380 --> 00:10:45,920
What is he doing?

223
00:10:53,260 --> 00:10:54,260
All right.

224
00:10:54,760 --> 00:10:55,900
Here we go.

225
00:10:57,420 --> 00:10:59,820
Feels like something big's about to happen.

226
00:11:03,980 --> 00:11:05,240
That's the way.

227
00:11:05,680 --> 00:11:06,740
Just like that.

228
00:11:07,460 --> 00:11:08,800
Flow right on through me.

229
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:10,680
Darkness.

230
00:11:10,680 --> 00:11:14,500
Come on.

231
00:11:15,420 --> 00:11:16,280
Give me more.

232
00:11:21,200 --> 00:11:22,760
What is that aura?

233
00:11:23,400 --> 00:11:25,400
It doesn't feel like magic at all.

234
00:11:26,100 --> 00:11:27,260
It's so strong.

235
00:11:27,760 --> 00:11:28,740
So fierce.

236
00:11:29,560 --> 00:11:32,160
It almost feels sinister.

237
00:11:33,620 --> 00:11:34,660
Get ready!

238
00:11:40,680 --> 00:11:42,360
Black Hurricane!

239
00:11:45,360 --> 00:11:45,680
Whoa.

240
00:11:46,020 --> 00:11:46,840
The cherry blossoms.

241
00:11:47,460 --> 00:11:47,780
Wait.

242
00:11:47,900 --> 00:11:48,540
Forget those.

243
00:11:48,600 --> 00:11:49,800
He'll destroy my traps.

244
00:11:53,800 --> 00:11:54,360
Wow.

245
00:11:54,640 --> 00:11:55,380
Us looks good.

246
00:11:55,540 --> 00:11:56,160
That attack.

247
00:11:56,380 --> 00:11:57,140
It's from before.

248
00:11:57,140 --> 00:12:07,780
It's the wiping out the fury blossoms bit by bit.

249
00:12:17,400 --> 00:12:17,920
Impossible.

250
00:12:18,280 --> 00:12:20,860
How'd that lowborn runt summon such a dreadful power?

251
00:12:20,860 --> 00:12:33,000
Look at that.

252
00:12:33,380 --> 00:12:34,240
He's pretty strong.

253
00:12:34,920 --> 00:12:36,200
I know that wasn't easy.

254
00:12:39,200 --> 00:12:39,720
Wow.

255
00:12:40,080 --> 00:12:41,040
That was amazing!

256
00:12:41,160 --> 00:12:41,840
Nice work!

257
00:12:42,080 --> 00:12:44,380
Do you have any idea what you've just done?

258
00:12:45,540 --> 00:12:47,120
You seem kind of pissed.

259
00:12:47,480 --> 00:12:49,440
I guess you really do care about these fights.

260
00:12:49,440 --> 00:12:54,500
Now, let's join forces and win this thing together!

261
00:12:55,780 --> 00:12:57,120
You rotten imbecile.

262
00:12:59,200 --> 00:13:02,240
What is this ugliness?

263
00:13:03,060 --> 00:13:04,760
What in the world happened?

264
00:13:05,140 --> 00:13:07,440
How did that commoner dispel all that magic?

265
00:13:08,900 --> 00:13:11,060
Asta will only get stronger from here on.

266
00:13:11,060 --> 00:13:13,820
And same goes for me.

267
00:13:14,400 --> 00:13:15,320
Very impressive.

268
00:13:15,540 --> 00:13:18,360
It would seem Asta's mastered yet another curious power.

269
00:13:18,580 --> 00:13:19,520
Open wide gate!

270
00:13:20,440 --> 00:13:22,620
Do you ever think before you act runt,

271
00:13:22,980 --> 00:13:26,140
all the time I spent setting traps is wasted effort now?

272
00:13:26,900 --> 00:13:28,180
It sure was.

273
00:13:28,580 --> 00:13:29,560
They're all gone.

274
00:13:29,980 --> 00:13:30,780
Rough, I know.

275
00:13:30,780 --> 00:13:33,940
But it happened.

276
00:13:34,740 --> 00:13:36,760
Time for you to give us a backup plan!

277
00:13:37,460 --> 00:13:39,480
One where all three of us can win this!

278
00:13:39,560 --> 00:13:39,820
Huh?

279
00:13:40,200 --> 00:13:41,260
You're a crafty guy.

280
00:13:41,340 --> 00:13:42,500
I'm sure you can think of something.

281
00:13:43,300 --> 00:13:46,900
Come up with a new underhanded plan and we'll beat those guys fair and square!

282
00:13:46,900 --> 00:13:51,040
You do realize that you're contradicting yourself, right?

283
00:13:51,980 --> 00:13:52,980
Thank goodness.

284
00:13:53,260 --> 00:13:55,080
Looks like the old Asta's back.

285
00:13:55,380 --> 00:13:56,360
We don't need a plan.

286
00:13:56,460 --> 00:13:59,200
That attack of yours should be more than enough to take out their team.

287
00:13:59,820 --> 00:14:00,820
So go get them.

288
00:14:02,660 --> 00:14:04,640
Totally would, but unfortunately for you,

289
00:14:04,720 --> 00:14:06,080
that move takes a lot out of me,

290
00:14:06,140 --> 00:14:08,720
so I'm gonna have to wait a while before I can whip it out again.

291
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:11,200
Why are you acting so damn happy about it?

292
00:14:11,640 --> 00:14:13,280
Seriously, are you sick in the head, kid?

293
00:14:13,280 --> 00:14:15,660
Don't you get it yet?

294
00:14:15,720 --> 00:14:17,600
I want us all to fight as a freaking team!

295
00:14:17,800 --> 00:14:20,260
So I don't care if you laid out all those traps yesterday.

296
00:14:20,680 --> 00:14:23,560
It's time you started treating me and Mimosa like real partners!

297
00:14:24,820 --> 00:14:27,100
We're fighting to get picked as royal knights.

298
00:14:27,260 --> 00:14:30,380
If we win, it'll be on us to take down the eye of the midnight sun.

299
00:14:30,520 --> 00:14:31,860
No one can fight them alone.

300
00:14:31,980 --> 00:14:33,580
Not me, not you, not anyone.

301
00:14:33,900 --> 00:14:36,240
There's only one way to beat a team as strong as that,

302
00:14:36,300 --> 00:14:37,000
and guess what?

303
00:14:37,180 --> 00:14:38,880
It's by making a team that's stronger!

304
00:14:41,600 --> 00:14:42,320
Look, son.

305
00:14:43,280 --> 00:14:46,240
Yes, my fellow magic knights are amazing people,

306
00:14:46,620 --> 00:14:48,220
but the thing that makes us amazing

307
00:14:48,220 --> 00:14:50,280
is that we never have to stand alone.

308
00:14:50,760 --> 00:14:53,620
We all trust that if we face death, we'll face it together.

309
00:14:58,140 --> 00:15:00,100
Look, the team we're up against right now

310
00:15:00,100 --> 00:15:02,280
has the vice-captain of the Coral Peacocks in it.

311
00:15:02,320 --> 00:15:04,480
He's a real piece of work, but he's also strong.

312
00:15:04,740 --> 00:15:07,740
We need to hit that jerk hard and fast with everything we've got!

313
00:15:07,740 --> 00:15:11,380
What the?

314
00:15:12,080 --> 00:15:15,020
Hey, if you don't like my ideas, then just say so next time!

315
00:15:15,080 --> 00:15:18,040
I want to join that royal guard like I want a pet tapeworm.

316
00:15:18,040 --> 00:15:22,000
But my goals aren't about to achieve themselves,

317
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:26,540
so I guess that leaves me with no choice but to put you to use, you little punk.

318
00:15:27,540 --> 00:15:30,040
I don't really care what your motive is.

319
00:15:30,100 --> 00:15:32,220
All that matters to me is that we fight together.

320
00:15:32,220 --> 00:15:37,880
As I'm sure you've noticed,

321
00:15:38,280 --> 00:15:40,060
my magic attribute is ash,

322
00:15:40,300 --> 00:15:42,060
and my specialty is trap magic.

323
00:15:42,060 --> 00:15:46,820
But it's not exactly easy to create large-scale traps

324
00:15:46,820 --> 00:15:48,380
like the ones from our last match.

325
00:15:49,060 --> 00:15:52,700
Bigger traps require a lot more time and magic power to get going,

326
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:54,580
but they're also far more effective.

327
00:15:55,100 --> 00:15:57,240
I told you I didn't get any sleep last night.

328
00:15:57,500 --> 00:15:59,180
Wait, that was actually true?

329
00:15:59,660 --> 00:16:03,200
You and your weird sword blew away a whole night of work just like that.

330
00:16:03,440 --> 00:16:04,860
Yeah, sorry about that,

331
00:16:04,860 --> 00:16:06,900
but we didn't really have a whole lot of options.

332
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:08,620
Let me think.

333
00:16:09,160 --> 00:16:11,740
There are some traps that I can pull off right now.

334
00:16:12,060 --> 00:16:13,160
Three, actually.

335
00:16:14,100 --> 00:16:15,060
Okay, what are they?

336
00:16:15,500 --> 00:16:17,040
First one's a snare trap.

337
00:16:17,340 --> 00:16:19,940
Touch the magic circle, and it roots you in place,

338
00:16:20,260 --> 00:16:21,140
then snares you.

339
00:16:21,280 --> 00:16:22,500
Cool, cool. Go on.

340
00:16:22,820 --> 00:16:24,480
Next up is the pitfall trap.

341
00:16:24,780 --> 00:16:26,180
It's pretty straightforward, too.

342
00:16:26,540 --> 00:16:29,000
You dig a hole and wait for your target to fall inside.

343
00:16:29,600 --> 00:16:30,360
Very nice.

344
00:16:31,240 --> 00:16:33,440
Trap type number three is the landmine.

345
00:16:33,860 --> 00:16:36,180
It triggers a simple attack spell on contact.

346
00:16:36,500 --> 00:16:37,720
Yeah, I remember that one.

347
00:16:38,180 --> 00:16:41,060
All of those traps will disappear once they've been set off.

348
00:16:41,060 --> 00:16:43,820
So unless I invest a lot of time and magic power in them,

349
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:45,320
we can't expect much payoff.

350
00:16:45,980 --> 00:16:47,920
Now, what'll it be, kid?

351
00:16:49,520 --> 00:16:51,600
Dear me, I can't believe it.

352
00:16:52,160 --> 00:16:57,400
To think that my perfectly beautiful spell was corrupted and destroyed by that peasant's insidious weapon.

353
00:16:57,940 --> 00:16:59,860
You know, I can't say I'm surprised.

354
00:16:59,860 --> 00:17:04,180
See, I knew that Aust had been practicing that move plenty.

355
00:17:04,780 --> 00:17:07,380
The kid put in the work, and now he's got an ace up his sleeve.

356
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:10,520
Maybe this will teach you not to underestimate commoners.

357
00:17:10,660 --> 00:17:12,420
Oh, side note, I'm one myself.

358
00:17:13,200 --> 00:17:14,040
Don't say it!

359
00:17:14,200 --> 00:17:16,020
You mean to tell me you're a commoner, too?

360
00:17:16,020 --> 00:17:19,160
Yeah, and if it mattered, you would have noticed.

361
00:17:19,600 --> 00:17:20,480
Oh, no!

362
00:17:20,940 --> 00:17:22,760
I could never fight beside a commoner.

363
00:17:22,800 --> 00:17:24,380
I would just end up being defiled.

364
00:17:27,560 --> 00:17:29,420
Hey, wait up, you damn narcissist!

365
00:17:29,580 --> 00:17:31,500
We already fought together once!

366
00:17:31,680 --> 00:17:33,360
What's it gonna hurt to do it one more time?

367
00:17:33,740 --> 00:17:34,700
There's no need.

368
00:17:34,880 --> 00:17:37,340
I have power enough to eliminate these fools by myself.

369
00:17:37,980 --> 00:17:39,860
You two stay there and protect the crystal.

370
00:17:39,860 --> 00:17:41,680
You know what?

371
00:17:41,800 --> 00:17:42,160
Fine.

372
00:17:42,360 --> 00:17:43,320
Do whatever you want.

373
00:17:43,700 --> 00:17:45,780
But if you think I won't do the same, guess again.

374
00:17:46,300 --> 00:17:47,320
Good grief.

375
00:17:47,660 --> 00:17:49,400
The male animal certainly is stupid.

376
00:17:49,520 --> 00:17:50,820
There's no doubt about that.

377
00:17:52,420 --> 00:17:53,620
Commoners are brutish.

378
00:17:53,880 --> 00:17:57,640
They are unclean, and they are fundamentally lacking in magic power.

379
00:17:58,540 --> 00:17:59,640
How shameful.

380
00:18:00,180 --> 00:18:02,660
He shouldn't even be allowed to share a stage with royalty,

381
00:18:02,660 --> 00:18:05,100
let alone to stand at our beautiful sides.

382
00:18:08,480 --> 00:18:09,440
There's Mimosa.

383
00:18:09,860 --> 00:18:11,400
Probably heading for our crystal.

384
00:18:12,420 --> 00:18:15,760
And I'm sensing that Zerk's fellow's magic power from right there.

385
00:18:16,180 --> 00:18:19,300
As for the human waste, I'm getting nothing from him.

386
00:18:19,760 --> 00:18:21,600
What in the world is he, and where?

387
00:18:25,120 --> 00:18:26,520
Hey, you want some crystal?

388
00:18:26,940 --> 00:18:27,900
Come and get it!

389
00:18:28,200 --> 00:18:29,980
There you are, you filthy urchin.

390
00:18:31,560 --> 00:18:33,000
Cherry blossom magic!

391
00:18:33,340 --> 00:18:35,620
Dance of the beautiful cherry blossom blades!

392
00:18:35,620 --> 00:18:48,680
These petals slipped through the smallest openings.

393
00:18:48,680 --> 00:18:48,700
These petals slipped through the smallest openings.

394
00:18:48,700 --> 00:18:52,440
You're really strong!

395
00:18:52,760 --> 00:18:54,340
Such ugly cowardice.

396
00:18:54,840 --> 00:18:56,240
You shans escaped me!

397
00:18:59,240 --> 00:19:00,480
Come kick my butt!

398
00:19:00,660 --> 00:19:02,160
Should be easy for a royal!

399
00:19:03,260 --> 00:19:05,960
It may be faint, but I still sense magic.

400
00:19:06,360 --> 00:19:08,360
This is an obvious attempt to entrap me.

401
00:19:08,360 --> 00:19:11,940
I can see through this plan with ease, you craven wretch.

402
00:19:12,540 --> 00:19:13,880
Cherry blossom magic!

403
00:19:14,340 --> 00:19:15,900
My beautiful clones!

404
00:19:15,900 --> 00:19:22,880
Run out of the traps!

405
00:19:26,440 --> 00:19:29,920
Did you really think you could stop me with such a shoddy plan?

406
00:19:29,920 --> 00:19:34,220
First, you chose to enter a cramped space which constrains your blade,

407
00:19:34,460 --> 00:19:37,120
and then you gave up your only escape route.

408
00:19:37,300 --> 00:19:38,600
I didn't think of that!

409
00:19:38,920 --> 00:19:40,860
If only I was his smartest royalty!

410
00:19:45,120 --> 00:19:46,240
Be gone!

411
00:19:46,740 --> 00:19:47,460
Commoner!

412
00:19:47,460 --> 00:20:02,160
Now, how could this be?

413
00:20:02,480 --> 00:20:04,880
My clones disposed of every trap spell in the area.

414
00:20:04,960 --> 00:20:05,940
I was sure of it.

415
00:20:08,600 --> 00:20:09,040
True.

416
00:20:11,260 --> 00:20:13,280
You've got a real good nose for magic,

417
00:20:13,400 --> 00:20:15,620
and you rely on it way too much, dumbass.

418
00:20:15,620 --> 00:20:18,600
See, we knew you'd be on the lookout for trap spells,

419
00:20:18,960 --> 00:20:21,440
so we dug this pit with plain old elbow grease.

420
00:20:23,240 --> 00:20:24,740
Who's dirty now, royal?

421
00:20:25,540 --> 00:20:28,740
They made this not with magic, but with effort and muscle.

422
00:20:29,580 --> 00:20:31,000
I should have expected this.

423
00:20:31,900 --> 00:20:33,280
You pathetic primitives.

424
00:20:33,580 --> 00:20:34,940
Still, I'll fly right out!

425
00:20:36,440 --> 00:20:39,220
I really hate to do this to Mimosa's big brother,

426
00:20:39,340 --> 00:20:41,100
but I'm gonna have to knock you out for a bit.

427
00:20:41,440 --> 00:20:43,580
Stay away from me, you filthy beast!

428
00:20:45,620 --> 00:21:02,560
I told you that you and me could make a good team.

429
00:21:03,040 --> 00:21:05,420
Well, for the record, I was only using you.

430
00:21:05,420 --> 00:21:08,660
It's so stupid, at least!

431
00:21:10,420 --> 00:21:10,680
Well, now it's given the time.

432
00:21:13,060 --> 00:21:14,760
minimum don't trust your ener過usions.

433
00:21:17,320 --> 00:21:19,020
You can check your hand at night!

434
00:21:22,220 --> 00:21:23,320
I'll see you in the minute so you don't trust your date.

435
00:21:28,020 --> 00:21:29,800
Number two weeks here,

436
00:21:30,380 --> 00:21:31,300
you will continue your dreams.

437
00:21:31,340 --> 00:21:31,820
Take care.

438
00:21:31,820 --> 00:22:01,800
Thank you.

439
00:22:01,820 --> 00:22:31,800
Thank you.

440
00:22:31,820 --> 00:22:33,820
Thank you.

441
00:23:02,220 --> 00:23:06,500
Never happy with the looks of his potential brides, he remained forever alone.

442
00:23:07,700 --> 00:23:11,640
In time, his warped personality drove everyone who could have loved him away.

443
00:23:12,080 --> 00:23:14,260
His twilight years were remarkably lonely.

444
00:23:14,760 --> 00:23:17,400
Ah, there's a sight for sore eyes.

445
00:23:17,760 --> 00:23:18,960
Oh, so pretty.

446
00:23:18,960 --> 00:23:20,780
You truly are beautiful.

447
00:23:21,260 --> 00:23:23,160
If I could just touch.

448
00:23:23,960 --> 00:23:27,040
And so my stupid brother met his miserable end.

449
00:23:27,280 --> 00:23:29,080
At least I was in beautiful company.

450
00:23:29,400 --> 00:23:32,800
If you don't stop fawning over your own face, I might just drown you myself.

451
00:23:32,800 --> 00:23:37,920
Friends, don't be ridiculous.

452
00:23:38,440 --> 00:23:41,460
I'm just using these people to reach my own goals, that's all.

453
00:23:41,920 --> 00:23:44,040
Black Clover, page 79.

454
00:23:44,640 --> 00:23:46,720
Mr. Delinquent versus Muscle Brains.

455
00:23:47,240 --> 00:23:48,980
My magic is trapping the unaware.

